id: pm-rlm-answer-invariants
title: Verify final answers with executable count membership and equality invariants
description: "Bounded declarative final answer contracts over a certified immutable SDK environment, with a typed SDK and native CLI, compact receipts, typed remedies and public no-git validation."
type: Feature
status: in_progress
priority: 2
tags[2]: answer-invariants,read-only
created_at: "2026-10-29T05:05:49.811Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-29T05:32:01.714Z"
author: codex-agent
acceptance_criteria: "A cited but numerically false count fails; complete and incomplete source cases remain distinct; checks execute without inference, arbitrary code or writes; the report separates verified facts from unsupported natural-language claims"
parent: pm-rlm-a1ih
comments[5]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-29T05:06:00.832Z",codex-agent,"Overlap recheck: core SDK exports certifyCompleteListResult/listAllComplete and live aggregate(options, global)/PmClient.aggregate(options), with no immutable item-array aggregate parameter. Existing package aggregateItems handles frozen scope count/distinct; reuse it rather than re-read a live corpus. pm-context packs criterion evidence, pm-evidence validates recorded coverage and pm-review reviews changes; none executes final-answer truth checks. Existing pm-rlm evidence validates witness identity/coverage, not numeric truth. Design: a strict versioned answer-plus-checks contract, read-only certified acquisition, independent pass/fail/unknown receipts, frozen-source digest, unverified natural-language answer. No writes, journal, import, export or sync path is introduced; no transaction isolation claim. Status selectors compare explicit configured values and infer no lifecycle meaning."
  "2026-10-29T05:17:26.463Z",codex-agent,"Implementation decision: listAllComplete source acquisition can populate SDK derived caches. Verification therefore accepts an explicit complete SDK environment, re-certifies and detaches it, and performs no tracker reads or writes. CLI takes contract and --environment JSON files. This preserves strict zero-write execution without pretending SDK cache writes are read-only. New source bounds reject sparse/oversized environments. Per-check failures and unavailable values remain independent. Public validation: verified public pm-lint revision, 12 items / 30 files, files and directories read-only, no git executable, tree unchanged; asserted 13 vs actual 12 fails, 3 facts pass, partial-source fixture yields 4 unknown, 1002-byte report, no model calls or verification writes. No import/export/sync, persistent state, idempotency keys, leases or journals are added."
  "2026-10-29T05:25:02.987Z",codex-agent,"Behavioral revert evidence: node test/answer-invariants-revert.ts passed three disposable-copy proofs. Replacing exact comparison with unconditional success fails the false-count regression; removing scope intersection fails scope regression; bypassing SDK certification fails incomplete-source regression. Each fixed baseline passes, each reverted function fails by assertion, and exact fixed bytes are restored and pass. Seeded coverage exercises 500 three-check contract sequences with old-input replay, CRLF variants, all supported scalar fields, configured custom statuses, parent/dependency preservation and random ambient focus, plus 500 invalid input and 500 output mutations. No package import/export/sync paths exist to extend. Full npm/Bun gate evidence will come from exact-head CI; local checks remain targeted on this shared host."
  "2026-10-29T05:29:13.488Z",codex-agent,"Native format parity: core TOON intentionally removes object nulls and empty lists. The new report therefore emits source.items=unknown for incomplete sources and verified_fact_ids=none when no fact passed, retaining nullable row cells for exact scalar absence. Added actual-host JSON/TOON round-trip assertions for complete and incomplete inputs. A source-shaped object is always re-certified through the SDK; no supplied completeness flag is trusted. Isolated-home strict tracker health passes; the inherited global extension installation has a host-version skew, so it is excluded from CI-parity health evidence."
  "2026-10-29T05:31:54.005Z",codex-agent,"Validation complete: pinned pm test --run --progress --timeout 600 passed the linked command node --test --test-concurrency=2 test/answer-invariants.test.ts: 11 passed, 0 failed, including native JSON/TOON parity for complete and incomplete sources, 500 model sequences, 500 invalid-input cases, 500 output mutations and concurrent immutable invocations. A prior 120-second shared-host deadline expired and is retained as missing evidence; the explicit 600-second retry supplies the passing receipt. Local typecheck, lint, build, docstrings (38 files, 181 declarations), zero-duplication gate and isolated-home strict health pass. Focused c8 measured both new modules at 100/100/100/100 before the final explicit absence markers; full unchanged-threshold npm/Bun evidence is delegated to exact-head CI. Boundaries: assertions certify only the supplied snapshot; prose and freshness remain unevaluated. No upstream CLI bug found; source-cache writes and TOON sparse object presentation are explicit integration boundaries."
